    "temporal_category": "event dating: a session timestamp plus a relative phrase ('yesterday', 'last Saturday', 'next month') resolves to a date. Same pattern as LongMemEval temporal-reasoning and GoodAI Jokes. No slot changes value; multi-hop questions aggregate consistent mentions (activities, camping places) without supersession.",
    "provenance": "LoCoMo is the only benchmark inspected where a memory's SOURCE affects gold — but as attribution, not conflict. The adversarial category (446 of 1,986, 22%) swaps the speaker: 'What did Caroline realize after her charity race?' when it was Melanie's race. The correct behaviour is to reject the premise; a system that stores memories without their speaker cannot. This is provenance in the sense of 'whose memory is this', not 'which source is entitled to overwrite'. It does not test Finding 2, and it is the nearest external handle on provenance found anywhere.",
    "types": "none; open-domain (category 3, 96) is commonsense, not state type"
